highlight.js (core build)
Version: 11.11.1
Licence: BSD-3-Clause
Source:  https://www.npmjs.com/package/highlight.js (LICENSE from the highlight.js@11.11.1 package)

This file is a custom bundle of highlight.js's core engine
(highlight.js/lib/core) plus the language grammars listed below, built with
esbuild (--bundle --minify --format=iife) so the whole thing self-hosts as one
dependency-free <script> with no CDN and no runtime fetch, matching every
other vendored library in this directory. No highlight.js source was
otherwise modified; only the set of languages included was chosen.

The exact entry module is checked in beside this file as
`highlight.core.entry.mjs`, so the bundle is reproducible rather than a blob
somebody once downloaded:

    npm install highlight.js@11.11.1 esbuild
    npx esbuild highlight.core.entry.mjs --bundle --minify --format=iife \
        --outfile=highlight.core.js

26 grammars are registered, and with the aliases each grammar declares that
covers every language a fenced block in this repo can name:

    bash (sh, zsh)      elixir (ex)         makefile (mk, mak)  shell (console)
    c (h)               go (golang)         php                 sql
    cpp (c++, cc, hpp)  http (https)        plaintext (text)    swift
    csharp (cs)         ini (toml)          python (py)         typescript (ts)
    diff (patch)        java (jsp)          ruby (rb)           xml (html, svg)
    dockerfile          javascript (js)     rust (rs)           yaml (yml)
                        json (jsonc)        kotlin (kt)

A block whose language falls through to plaintext is a defect, not a style
choice — `scripts/check-docs-chrome.mjs` fails the build if any fence in
`docs/` names a language this bundle cannot highlight.

